From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:17:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] test: keep API and track-selection tests independent of
 hardware probes

Exercise automatic hardware selection separately with recorded GPU fixtures. The existing suite treats normal unsupported-device probe errors as a failure.

Assisted-by: gpt-6.1-sol via Codex
---
 test/libmpv_common.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/test/libmpv_common.h b/test/libmpv_common.h
index 50e2c84..ba26c77 100644
--- a/test/libmpv_common.h
+++ b/test/libmpv_common.h
@@ -157,6 +157,8 @@ MP_UNUSED static inline void check_string(const char *property, const char *expe
 static inline void initialize(void)
 {
     set_property_string("vo", "null");
+    // These API and track-selection tests must also run without a GPU.
+    set_property_string("hwdec", "no");
     set_property_string("ao", "null");
     int ret = mpv_request_log_messages(ctx, "debug");
     if (ret < 0)
